			<div class="content" id="post-content-2387029">
									

<p>This may be the most actually artistic anart skip I have read.</p>
<p>I have two small quibbles:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>resemble the original paintings to an anomalous degree of accuracy</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't think a perfect forgery is inherently anomalous. It ought to be possible to use very accurate microscopic cameras and very precise computer controlled paint deposition to do this in real life. I remember a Scientific American article about this in the 80s, surely it's even more doable today. Obviously his methods <em>are</em> anomalous, but I don't think that the forgeries are themselves so.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>radiocarbon dating of paints</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since these are all recent 19th and 20th century paintings, radiocarbon dating isn't likely to produce accurate results anyway.</p>

